<title>UK: Rolls wins Nat Grid infrastructure contract.</title>
<headline>Rolls wins Nat Grid infrastructure contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>British aero engine maker Rolls-Royce Plc said on Wednesday its Reyolle Projects company had won a 5.0 million stg contract from National Grid to upgrade supply systems in the northwest of England.</p>
<p>In a statement the company said the work would be carried out in phased stages in the Liverpool and Preston areas with final completion by the end of 1997.</p>
<p>It was the fifth such contract won by Reyolle in a week, Rolls noted, coming after a series of switchgear orders from the large British power distribution company.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
